        insight: `Sofia applied the hierarchy correctly: when the checklist and genuine wellbeing conflict, wellbeing wins, and the adjustment is absorbed professionally elsewhere rather than passed on to the guest or the next booking. Note what she protected: the full hands-on duration, the guest's dignity and the schedule's integrity, by communicating with the coordinator instead of silently running late. Note also what she exercised: judgement about a real need, not casual flexibility. Had an inspector been on her couch that afternoon, the humanity of the response would have scored, because graciousness and genuine care are standards too. Judgement over the exception, standards over the routine, is the five-star signature.`,
